WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.102
City employees have faced consequences

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:03.670
in the wake of Nichols killing.

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.205
Of the latest, two EMTs

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:06.072
and a fire department

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:07.440
lieutenant have now been fired.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.009
So that's three in the fire department

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:10.443
and a seventh Memphis

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:12.645
officer has been relieved of duty.

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:13.546
Last week,

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:15.382
five of those seven officers were charged

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:17.083
with second degree murder and assault

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:18.184
for Nichols death.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:18.885
CNN's Ryan

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:20.520
Young has the latest from Memphis.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.021
Also here,

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:21.821
CNN chief

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:22.589
law enforcement

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:24.858
and intelligence analyst John Miller.

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:28.361
Ryan, first, the discrepancies

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:30.196
between the video

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.531
and this initial report.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:33.233
Talk to us about them.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:34.601
Yeah,

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:35.935
something that we're still digging into.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:36.669
And of course, you guys

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:37.971
can ask John about this later.

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:39.172
But I've been talking to Memphis

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:41.307
Police Department officers today,

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:42.242
and they've been telling me that

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:44.277
when you file an initial police report,

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:46.179
you also include a use of force,

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:48.548
part of the report as well.

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:49.883
So if you had to escalate

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:50.283
maybe go

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.551
hands on or use

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:52.285
some type of force,

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:53.253
you usually include

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:54.621
that in the police report.

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:55.855
But these discrepancies

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:57.023
kind of stand out to us

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:57.490
as we've

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:58.992
watched this video over and over.

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:00.260
We'll take you through some of them.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.162
It says Nichols was an aggravated

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:03.163
assault suspect.

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:05.365
So that stood out to us as well.

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:06.166
And then he said it was

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:07.834
he was sweating profusely

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.903
and irate upon exiting the vehicle.

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:11.204
As we watch that video,

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.405
you saw the officers

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:13.673
actually approached that car

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:14.774
with a lot of force.

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:16.476
And then it says Nichols grabbed

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:18.111
for Detective Martin's gun.

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:20.914
And then Martin listed as a victim.

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:22.182
In this case, of course,

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:24.084
we don't see that initial pool

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:25.452
for any officer's weapon.

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:27.020
And then says Nichols pulled

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:28.822
on an officer's duty belt.

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:30.623
And there is no mention of the kicking

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:31.891
or punching of him.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.893
And again, after talking to an officer

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:34.260
who's worked

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.161
in this police department

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.329
for quite some time,

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:38.064
he said that would be listed

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:39.666
in that incident. Report at some time.

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:40.166
Of course,

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:40.667
not only have

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.135
we called to see the full report

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:43.403
that was initially put in.

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:45.271
We also have asked for that seventh

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:46.239
officer name.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:48.007
It hasn't been released just yet.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.476
So there's still a lot of questions

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:51.344
surrounding this initial report

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:52.445
that has come out.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:52.712
Okay.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.280
So, John, are discrepancies

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.282
like this in police reports common?

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:56.516
Well,

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:57.517
there's nothing common

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:58.485
about this incident.

00:01:58.485 --> 00:02:00.453
Because the report is

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.322
does not reflect what happened.

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:04.591
So it's more than discrepancies.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:05.458
But, Alisyn,

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.092
it seems

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:08.161
as if they have built into the narrative

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:10.330
a series of justifications.

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:11.097
And it's interesting

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:12.432
that you hear them mouth

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:13.199
some of those

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:15.235
at the end of the beating on tape

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:17.337
as if they're building a story that

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:19.072
that goes somewhere

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.039
other than we dragged

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:20.907
the guy out of a car

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:21.841
and started beating him

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:22.442
and didn't stop

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:24.911
until he was in a in a fatal car.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:25.578
But he grabbed the gun.

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:26.279
I think he grabbed the gun.

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:26.846
I think he grabbed

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:27.080
like it

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.314
starts to take on a life of its own

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:29.682
even more than that.

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.951
Because when you heard them talking

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.987
and that scene we just played,

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:35.188
one of them says,

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:37.257
you know, I said, hey, brother.

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:37.857
And you know,

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.692
he came out of the car and bam.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:42.295
Now we've all seen that first video

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:44.364
right there screaming at him

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:45.865
before he's ever out of the car

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:47.267
and he's saying, what did I do?

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:47.934
What did I do?

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:50.003
I'm getting on the ground. Okay. Okay.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.605
So they're they're constructing

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:54.340
they're constructing a false narrative

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.242
that is false from the beginning,

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:57.510
not just the elements

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.212
they add at the end, but they all

00:02:59.212 --> 00:02:59.913
they also know

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.014
that they're being recorded,

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:02.415
that there's a body cam,

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:04.517
that both is picking up the story,

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:06.653
but also has the incident

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:08.821
that doesn't reconcile

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:09.956
with what they're explaining.

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:12.225
Great question. But it cuts both ways.

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:13.660
They know that the body camera

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.561
is going to be blocked.

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:16.663
There's all kinds of chaos and confusion,

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.531
not everything is going to be recorded.

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:20.166
So you can see it plainly.

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:22.202
So they are building that narrative

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:23.670
while they are still recording

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:24.237
because they know

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:25.238
they're still recording.

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:26.472
So they're trying to say.

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:27.707
When you look at this tape,

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.709
here's the parts you might have missed.

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:30.977
Here's something that they didn't

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:31.978
account for,

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:34.180
the pull camera, which captured it all.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.215
Clearly,

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.883
there's something else here

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:37.684
in the report.

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:38.851
They say

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:39.652
a lieutenant

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:40.486
and they name him

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:41.287
and give his

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:42.488
his shield number

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.757
made the scene indicating he was there.

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:48.728
This is the first time we have ever heard

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:50.697
about a supervisor

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:53.132
to ranks up having been present.

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:54.634
So there's going to be a real question

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.269
about, okay,

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:57.637
this lieutenant got there

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:59.872
when and was there for what part of this.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:01.708
Brian, we know

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:03.910
his funeral is scheduled for tomorrow.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.044
So what do we know about that?

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.448
Yeah, we do know that tomorrow

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:09.983
Breonna Taylor's mother will be here.

00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:11.451
George Floyd's brother will be here.

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:12.218
We just learned

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:12.685
the vice

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.721
president will be here at the funeral

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:15.488
tomorrow.

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:16.556
Put all this together

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:17.590
with a news conference

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.825
that's supposed to happen

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:20.426
just in the next few hours.

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:21.728
So much still happening here

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:23.596
and obviously with this investigation.

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:24.998
People asking questions about that

00:04:24.998 --> 00:04:26.332
initial incident report

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:27.333
and just how many times

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.035
this Scorpion unit was involved

00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:30.003
in incidents

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:31.204
that haven't been reported

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:32.972
or gone this far.

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:33.373
Okay.

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:34.340
Ryan Young, John Miller,

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.242
thank you both very much.

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:37.343
Joining us now, Patrice

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:38.911
Robinson, a member of the Memphis

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:39.946
City Council.

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:41.581
Councilwoman, thank you for your time.

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:42.181
I want to pick up

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:43.950
where that conversation left off.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.952
We know now that there were

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:47.920
there are two additional officers

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.022
who have been relieved of duty.

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:51.024
We know one of them.

00:04:51.024 --> 00:04:52.091
His name was released.

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:53.593
The other was not

00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:54.394
of this

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:56.596
Preston Hemphill, the sixth officer.

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:59.032
He was recorded saying, I hope they stomp

00:04:59.032 --> 00:05:01.167
his ass. He's not been fired.

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:02.802
Can any of the officers

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:04.170
stay on board

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.272
with the Memphis Police Department,

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:08.174
any of the officers who were involved

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:09.676
in this this incident

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:13.046
I do believe

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:13.846
that we're going

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:15.848
to be as transparent as possible.

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:18.451
And I know that we're going to be fair

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:19.085
as possible.

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:20.019
But I don't see

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:23.222
anybody on that street at the time.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.459
Should work for the police department.

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:28.394
Now, I may be wrong.

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:30.463
The law might say something differently.

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:31.864
But if they were there

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:33.633
and they didn't intervene,

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:36.803
they're all in the same boat together.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:38.504
Hmm. Yeah.

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:41.474
The question is, can trust be restored

00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:42.942
if that Officer Hempel

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:46.412
shows up on a scene and local people know

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:47.280
that he's the person who said,

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:48.581
I hope they stop his ass.

00:05:48.581 --> 00:05:50.516
What degree of trust and confidence

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:51.551
will they have

00:05:51.551 --> 00:05:52.785
that they will be

00:05:52.785 --> 00:05:53.453
taken care of

00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:55.555
within the bounds of the law?

00:05:55.655 --> 00:05:56.255
Do you have

00:05:56.255 --> 00:06:00.093
a concern about the lack of disclosure

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:01.761
of these additional officers

00:06:01.761 --> 00:06:03.563
being relieved of duty?

00:06:03.563 --> 00:06:05.465
Not on the first day when it happened,

00:06:05.465 --> 00:06:06.666
but several weeks later.

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:10.236
I have a concern

00:06:10.236 --> 00:06:11.771
starting from the beginning

00:06:11.771 --> 00:06:14.707
of what we saw on the video.

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:16.442
And you have made it very clear,

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:18.644
I heard in your last segment

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:21.180
that when they approached him in his car,

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.648
they just snatched him out.

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:24.550
We have no idea.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:26.819
Nobody knows why he was that.

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:29.956
They said it was a trap violation.

00:06:30.056 --> 00:06:32.191
We don't know that for sure either.

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:33.860
Yes, I am concerned.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:34.961
I'm concerned

00:06:34.961 --> 00:06:36.963
that all the information

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:39.031
did not come at the same time.

00:06:39.332 --> 00:06:41.367
But I know the community

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:42.468
have been pressuring

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:43.636
the police department

00:06:43.636 --> 00:06:45.838
to issue everything they can and know

00:06:45.872 --> 00:06:47.774
that they're doing investigations.

00:06:47.774 --> 00:06:49.075
We want to make sure

00:06:49.075 --> 00:06:49.842
that we were

00:06:49.842 --> 00:06:51.878
as transparent as possible

00:06:52.044 --> 00:06:53.679
and we made sure

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:55.081
that we were getting information

00:06:55.081 --> 00:06:58.084
that two individuals as it I mean,

00:06:58.117 --> 00:06:59.485
as soon as we could

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:01.387
get it out of the office.

00:07:01.387 --> 00:07:04.290
Now, we knew everybody

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:05.691
that looked at the video,

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:08.060
knew the other people were involved

00:07:08.428 --> 00:07:09.295
we didn't know how

00:07:09.295 --> 00:07:11.063
they were going to be addressed.

00:07:11.063 --> 00:07:12.465
But now we are seeing that

00:07:12.465 --> 00:07:13.966
they are being addressed.

00:07:13.966 --> 00:07:17.069
And my concern at this point is

00:07:17.236 --> 00:07:19.138
what are we going to do

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:20.740
and what will the law say

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:23.810
that we need to do moving forward?

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:25.077
And how will the D.A.

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:27.146
plug in at this point?

00:07:27.146 --> 00:07:27.814
So, obviously,

00:07:27.814 --> 00:07:29.682
there's a question of culture there,

00:07:29.682 --> 00:07:31.050
not only within this now

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.452
disbanded Scorpion unit,

00:07:32.452 --> 00:07:34.020
but these officers

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.822
were wearing body cameras.

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:37.323
They were in a neighborhood

00:07:37.323 --> 00:07:40.326
there could have been cell phone cameras.

00:07:40.326 --> 00:07:41.461
The pole camera was there.

00:07:41.461 --> 00:07:42.128
And that didn't

00:07:42.128 --> 00:07:43.529
deter or discourage

00:07:43.529 --> 00:07:45.932
any of the action that we saw.

00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:47.567
On the question of culture,

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:48.801
is Chief Davis

00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:50.436
the right person to continue

00:07:50.436 --> 00:07:51.671
to lead this department

00:07:51.671 --> 00:07:52.605
as it tries

00:07:52.605 --> 00:07:54.874
to shift to obviously a different culture

00:07:57.243 --> 00:07:59.479
I believe she is the right person

00:07:59.846 --> 00:08:01.347
to help them shift

00:08:01.347 --> 00:08:03.082
to a different culture,

00:08:03.082 --> 00:08:04.417
because you can't take people

00:08:04.417 --> 00:08:06.152
that are already in the culture

00:08:06.152 --> 00:08:07.420
and utilize them

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:08.421
to change the culture

00:08:08.421 --> 00:08:09.689
that they're used to.

00:08:09.689 --> 00:08:11.724
It really doesn't make a lot of

00:08:11.724 --> 00:08:13.493
sense, but we don't have

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:15.027
a lot

00:08:15.027 --> 00:08:16.562
of bad players but we

00:08:16.562 --> 00:08:18.164
know we do have something

00:08:18.164 --> 00:08:20.733
and we don't have as many as

00:08:22.201 --> 00:08:24.403
the public probably thinks.

00:08:24.403 --> 00:08:26.439
And my heart goes out

00:08:26.606 --> 00:08:28.140
not just to their family,

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:30.243
but to the families of all the officers,

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:32.345
knowing that their fathers,

00:08:32.345 --> 00:08:33.145
their brothers,

00:08:33.145 --> 00:08:37.316
their that their own people are there

00:08:37.316 --> 00:08:39.151
each and every day working.

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:40.887
And they want to see their fathers

00:08:40.887 --> 00:08:41.821
at the end of the day

00:08:41.821 --> 00:08:42.688
or their husbands

00:08:42.688 --> 00:08:44.323
at the end of the day or their brothers

00:08:44.323 --> 00:08:45.558
at the end of the day.

00:08:45.558 --> 00:08:48.761
And I do believe that Chief Davis

00:08:48.761 --> 00:08:50.963
has moved us in the right direction.

00:08:51.197 --> 00:08:52.832
And there was nothing

00:08:52.832 --> 00:08:55.368
she could have done to have stopped

00:08:55.368 --> 00:08:56.969
what happened on that day.

00:08:56.969 --> 00:08:58.471
It was tragic.

00:08:58.471 --> 00:09:00.806
Those men make very poor decisions

00:09:01.007 --> 00:09:02.742
from the beginning of the video

00:09:02.742 --> 00:09:05.678
that I saw all the way to the end.

00:09:06.279 --> 00:09:06.546
All right.

00:09:06.546 --> 00:09:07.113
Memphis City

00:09:07.113 --> 00:09:08.514
Councilwoman Patrice Robinson,

00:09:08.514 --> 00:09:09.649
thank you so much for your time.

00:09:11.417 --> 00:09:12.118
Thank you.

